From: xPDFSDK team <noreply@xpdfsdk.local>
Date: 2026-06-19
Subject: [PATCH ship-0014] Cache Veloce Form path display lists

Background
==========
The r7 path display-list patch made the `/Meta20` Form XObject render through a
compact native path list, but it still compiled that list inside every visible
render call. Device logs showed the problem clearly: even a 256px preview paid
roughly 1.1-1.3s of `compileMs` before replay could begin.

This patch
==========
1. Adds a small process-local LRU cache for compiled `NativePathDisplayList`
   instances.
2. Keys the cache by document pointer, `CPDF_PageObjectHolder*`, holder
   dictionary object number, and the path-smoothing render option that affects
   compiled paint state.
3. Reuses the compiled list on subsequent preview/tile renders so the visible
   render path can replay rather than recompile the Form.
4. Adds `cache=hit|miss` telemetry to the existing `VelocePathDL` log line.
5. Checks cancellation during compile every 64 scanned objects. A cancelled
   compile returns `kCancelled` instead of falling back to legacy rendering.

This is intentionally still conservative. Unsupported Forms remain ineligible
and fall back before drawing. The cache is bounded to 32 entries and does not
change public PDFium API.

diff --git a/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp b/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp
index 951822a85..815b4d4ce 100644
--- a/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp
+++ b/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp
@@ -9,7 +9,10 @@
